# Single source of truth for the pinned toolchain.
#
# Read by portable/setup.sh (via `source`) and by .github/workflows/release.yml
# (both jobs). Keeping one copy avoids the platform skew this file replaced:
# release.yml and setup.sh each carried their own pins, so macOS shipped a
# Node v22.16.0 / v22.22.1 hybrid while Windows was on a third version.
#
# Format: KEY=value, no spaces, no quotes (parsed by both bash and PowerShell).

# Windows embedded interpreter. 3.11 stopped shipping embeddable builds after
# 3.11.9 (Apr 2024, security-only since), so 3.13 is the only line still
# publishing one. Upstream hermes-agent requires >=3.11,<3.14.
PYTHON_EMBED_VERSION=3.13.17

# Node.js Active LTS. hermes-web-ui declares engines.node >=23.0.0.
NODE_VERSION=v24.22.1

# uv. Must be >=0.8 to honour upstream's [tool.uv.exclude-newer-package]
# table; older versions silently ignore it and resolve the wrong versions.
UV_VERSION=0.12.24

# Chat Web UI. Pinned deliberately: upstream ships 2-4 releases a week, so an
# unpinned install makes every build a different product.
HERMES_WEB_UI_VERSION=0.7.39

# The AI engine itself, as an upstream release tag. Leaving this unpinned is
# what let ~21.5k commits of drift land in one go and break the build unnoticed.
# The weekly canary run builds against upstream main instead, so drift shows up
# as a failed scheduled run rather than a failed release.
#
# THE NEXT BUMP MOVES PYTHON_EMBED_VERSION TO 3.14 IN THE SAME CHANGE.
# v2026.9.24 (0.21.5) is the last release that runs on our Python 3.13: right
# after tagging it, upstream main went 3.14-only. Every core dependency now
# carries `; python_version >= '3.14'`, so on 3.13 the engine installs with its
# core requirements skipped (only what the extras pull in arrives) and dies on
# `import ruamel`. 0.21.5 itself still requires <3.14, so there is no version
# both can share -- the engine and Python move together. Embeddable 3.14
# builds exist (3.14.8). tools/update_pins.py holds back a release whose core
# dependencies are mostly gated to a newer Python (the shape upstream main has
# now), so it will not propose the engine half alone.
# Until that move, the canary is red for this reason, not for noise.
# v2026.9.24 == hermes-agent 0.21.5
HERMES_AGENT_REF=v2026.9.24
